  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIRAS Own Implementation - Regional Migration Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Migrants, refugees and the population of host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Migration and displacement are important social dynamics in the Horn of Africa. Migration can be a source of integration, development, prosperity and the exchange of ideas and values. Legal and safe mobility of people is therefore promoted in the IGAD region. However, if migration is driven by structural challenges like poverty, conflicts and lack of economic opportunities and happens out of necessity, it is often unsafe and irregular, exposing people to a variety of risks. It can create challenges both in the places of origin (e.g. loss of young, ambitious people) as well as in the places of transit and destination (e.g. increased pressure on public infrastructure and natural resources). Therefore, it is important to reduce migration out of necessity, i.e. the perceived or actual need to migrate as a coping strategy to escape hardship or lack of (economic) opportunities. The Regional Migration Fund (RMF) project was developed by IGAD and implemented by NIRAS with the goal of ensuring that &quot;The living conditions and economic opportunities for migrants, refugees, and host communities are improved and social cohesion is strengthened &quot;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">a) Economic potential of the border areas along migration routes is enhanced and employment for migrants and local communities in particular youth has been created.

b) The socio-economic inclusion of refugees and host communities in protracted displacement situations is enhanced.</narrative>
  </description>
